   "prompt": "Opus review (medium, cap bypass): in tools/lanes.mjs claimLaneSlots and its caller in tools/swarm.mjs, slots are granted in the order of the waiters list but the scheduler lines grants up against pending, which is waiters with cancelled jobs removed. If a job is cancelled while the claim is in flight the lists no longer line up, so a slot labelled for one endpoint or for an agency or non-agency job can go to a different job, and per-endpoint slots or the agency cap can be exceeded; a legitimately granted job can also lose its slot. Fix: have claimLaneSlots return each grant tagged with the job id (waiter identity), and have the scheduler match grants to pending jobs by id, releasing any grant whose job is no longer pending. Add tests in tests/local-lane-review.test.mjs: a cancelled job in the middle of the waiter list must not shift endpoint or agency labels, and a grant for a cancelled job is released. Keep tests/local-lane.test.mjs, tests/lanes.test.mjs, tests/lanes-run.test.mjs, tests/router.test.mjs, tests/api-workers.test.mjs passing.",
